    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Tomorrow's meetings, and yesterday's no-shows\nAspire books consultations, Splunk demos and career calls across\neight calendars. A reminder the day before is the cheapest way to\ncut no-shows; catching the ones that were missed is how a lead\ngets a second chance instead of going quiet.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "092144703665",
      "name": "1. Tomorrow's meetings, and yesterday's no-shows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Decide who gets a nudge and what got missed\nAn appointment still marked booked hours after it should have\nfinished was almost certainly a no-show. Marking it is what lets\nanyone ask how often it happens, per calendar.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "548509870282",
      "name": "2. Decide who gets a nudge and what got missed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        640,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Remind, or record the miss\nThe reminder finally uses the template that has sat unused since\nthe first build. A no-show becomes a task, because someone who\nbooked and did not arrive is still interested \u2014 they just need\nrescheduling.",
        "height": 510,
        "width": 1520,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "895013851435",
      "name": "3. Remind, or record the miss",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1200,
        140
      ]
